% Add one BibTeX entry per source actually checked and logged in AI/SOURCES.md.
% Never add an entry for a source you have not opened; the librarian role in
% AGENTS.md treats a search result as a lead only, until checked.
%
% BibTeX scans this file for the at-sign character, wherever it appears, and
% tries to parse an entry starting there, even inside a comment. For that
% reason this file names the character instead of writing it, below.
%
% An entry starts with the at-sign character directly followed by the entry
% type and an opening brace, for example: article, followed directly by
% {example2024, then fields such as author, title, journal, year, volume,
% and pages, each as name = {value}, separated by commas, closed with a
% final brace.
